Greece in 60 Seconds · History in 60 Seconds series · Silkscreen Travel Poster style

Picture: drawn in code (Canvas 2D). Print engine engine/silk.js from the Lemo-Opuscar library (MIT).
Landmarks (a terraced palace with tapering columns, an assembly hill, a temple of columns on its rock, a phalanx and galleys,
a fortress over a harbour, tall sailing ships and a chapel, a marble stadium, a white island village with windmills and a ferry)
are original stylised silhouettes drawn as simple paths, not traced from photographs. No logos, no flags or emblems, no maps or borders.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/):
  Big Shoulders Display — Patric King / Google Fonts
  Outfit — Rodrigo Fuenzalida / Google Fonts

Voice: Kokoro-82M v1.0 (hexgrad, Apache-2.0) via kokoro-onnx, voice bm_george. Checked with faster-whisper (MIT), model base.en.

Music (original score, music/compose.py): bouzouki by physical modelling (core/audio/pluck.py, Lemo-Opuscar, MIT);
lyra, daouli and toubeleki synthesised in code. No samples.
Sound (mix.py): paper swish, stamps, a stylus scratching, surf, wind, gulls, an assembly, cicadas, marching feet, a stadium crowd,
a ferry horn: synthesised in code.
Mastering: FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL) via imageio-ffmpeg.

Facts and sources: FACTS.md.
